    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0437" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3978: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-24T10:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                                1921—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 24—1:28
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>254. From Peking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 23rd, 4 p.m. Expected storm against Peking is breaking. Following
                            upon series of recent defeats Kwangsi forces at hands Kwangtung, Hunan
                            is now moving troops against Wuchang. Szechuan and other wavering
                            provinces will probably join in attack <pb facs="0438" n="314"
                                xml:id="pg314"/> on Peking unless Hunan is decisively defeated in
                            which event Wu Pei-fu<anchor n="2" xml:id="d272-f1"/> in Honan holds
                            keys to situation. Allegiance of all Yangtze Provinces very doubtful.
                            Premier tendered his resignation 21st; not yet accepted. Repeat to
                            Department as Legation’s 271.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d272-f1" n="2" xml:id="d272-f1-content">
                <p>Vice Inspector General of Chihli, Shantung, and Honan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
